#27600
Everwar Mountain~
This area is an exp/quest area for levels 20-50, exp is for levels 20-45 while
those brave souls he try it can go for the quest.  The book of the godwar best
describes this horrible battle of the races.  The book of the godwar is resting
on a table here.  Built by Jamar and links to Plains of Xev at 39543
~
276 0 0 0 0 0 255 0
D5
~
~
0 0 1200
E
book godwar~

   Since the beginning of time when the mortal races first learned of death
they have searched for the key to immortality.  After awhile the gods found the
mortals quest for such unreachable goals to be of amusement to them.  They
decided they would assist the silly mortals in their quests.  After all no wars
had taken place for over 200 years and all the races were beginning to show
signs of overpopulation.  The gods created a magical item capable of removing
years of age from the mortals and found this to be very funny.  For while they
might go back in age all they were accomplishing was having more years to
search and feel the failure of their lives in never reaching their dreams.  
But the gods knew that this alone was no fun to them, so they placed the item
on top of a lone mountain in the middle of all the kingdoms.  They proclaimed
the race that was the first to the top and found the relic would be given a
taste of immortality.  The kings of each race thought that this was meant for
them alone since the gods sent messengers to each king proclaiming him as the
chosen of the gods.  The kings after years of peace had plenty of able bodies
warriors and felt they had plenty of warriors young and old willing to die for
them.  And so it was that the races of the Humans, Dwarves, Elves, Trolls,
Ogres and Gnomes descended upon the mountain with their armies in full force.
They each set camp at a different bases of the mountain and proceded onward.  
All the while the peasents and nobility had set up viewing and gambling places
to see what race would reach the top first and forever live as the gods.  The
wars were expected to be over within a very short time, alas 25 years later no
race can claim any kind of victory.  All the races are beginning to show the
ill effects of war as their are not enough young people to tend to the farms
and kingdoms for each race and each army is getting close to complete and utter
defeat.  Only the kings in their lust for this holy object refuse to listen to
any of their advisors and have gone mad with desire.    
~
S
#27601
A worn road~
   The road is nothing like was in the forest now, deep mud filled ruts run all
along the road now.  Turra no longer cares for the road and until all the
armies leave will not venture out from the city.  The battle for Mt Everwar has
been going on for so many years now that most younger citizens have never known
anything but war.    
~
